WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.890
SPEAKER: Natural
Language API can

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.370
be used to perform sentiment,
entity, and syntax analysis

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.850
on text.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.710
Let's just see how to
use Natural Language

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.960
API with C Shell.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.960
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.690
and the service icon
exists to make API calls.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.870
Both are explained in the
code lab in the video notes.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.790
In Cloud Shell, let's create a
simple .net console app and add

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.960
Natural Language API Nougat
package to the project.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.310
Open the Code Editor and
navigate to program.cs.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.130
We will perform sentiment
analysis on a piece of text.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.590
Reference Natural
Language API library.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.255
Create language service client.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.950
Call analyze
sentiment on the text.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.555
Get the sentiment, and
finally, print the results.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.350
Let's run the app.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.130
There you go.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.320
You just performed
sentiment analysis

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.010
using Natural Language API.

